    <GaugingStation location="Moor House" name="Sike Hill" number="25810">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">A V-notch weir level only station, affected by heavy silting. Peak flow only station. Closed December 1962. Not suitable for QMED estimation from catchment descriptors because of very small catchment size.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Zero of V notch is 0.551m on staff gauge. Imprecise at low flows, and inaccurate at high flows once water level rises above the top of the V notch at 0.332m above gauge zero. At 0.361m above the zero of the V bypassing begins over the horizontal top of the weir board, and on the left bank, bypassing the recorder. Single peak flow theoretical rating applied throughout. Confirmed by check gaugings.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">A V-notch weir with stilling pool and water level recorder. Prone to heavy silting, with 80 cubic feet removed in five years. Peak flow only station. Station closed 31/12/1962.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Runoff likely to be low during wintry conditions. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in August 2024 (WINFAP Files v13).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">No known artificial influences.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">A small upland catchment draining into the Tees via the Trout Beck. During the experimental period of recording the catchment was artificially surface drained. Accurate spatial data processing of catchment descriptors is not possible because of the very small catchment size.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff"/>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="QMED is contained within V notch, plus check gaugings confirm rating to above QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Although gauged beyond AMAX3, high flows are not contained within the structure of the weir making rating extrapolation unreliable." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
